# Testing

## Layout

- Mirror source paths under `tests/` (e.g. `tests/lib/org-permissions.test.ts` for `src/lib/org-permissions.ts`)
- Security tests live in `tests/security/` — IDOR, tenant isolation, rate limiting
- Integration tests live in `tests/integration/` — Supertest against Express app
- Helpers live in `tests/helpers/` — `test-app.ts`, `test-db.ts`, `auth.ts`

## Unit tests

- Framework: Vitest (Node environment — no jsdom)
- Run: `pnpm test` (watch) or `pnpm test:ci` (CI single run)
- Name tests after user outcomes, not function signatures
- Mock Prisma in unit tests; use real SQLite DB in integration tests

## Integration tests

- Framework: Vitest + Supertest
- Run: `pnpm test:integration` or included in `make pre-push`
- Use `createTestApp()` from `tests/helpers/test-app.ts`
- Auth: sign up/sign in via Better Auth `/api/auth/*` endpoints; use `request.agent()` for cookies
- Test env vars set in `vitest.setup.ts` at project root

## Test environment

```
DATABASE_URL=file:./prisma/test.db
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=test-secret-min-32-chars-long!!
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4000
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:3000
NODE_ENV=test
```

## CI gates

| Gate | Command | Includes |
|------|---------|----------|
| PR / local check | `make check` | lint, format, typecheck, security-audit, vitest unit |
| Pre-push / CI | `make pre-push` | `make check` + integration tests |

- `make ci` is identical to `make pre-push`
- Never use `--no-verify` unless explicitly requested (see `git-hooks.mdc`)

## Coverage targets

- ≥80% on `src/lib/tenant-guard.ts`, `src/lib/org-permissions.ts`, middleware
- Run `vitest --coverage` in CI (optional artifact upload)
